# @ryph/host — environment for the single-process local deployment (`bun run up`).
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust; every variable keeps the same name, default, and
# semantics as the standalone services, so the per-package docs own the details.

# ── Listeners ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Control plane: user + runner surfaces, auth, provider-key CRUD.
#RYPH_PORT=7411
# Model-proxy data plane — its own listener; agent containers dial it over the network.
#RYPH_MODEL_PROXY_PORT=7420
# MCP-gateway data plane — the same, one credential class over: what containers dial as "the
# MCP server".
#RYPH_MCP_GATEWAY_PORT=7430

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one shared database for every mounted module's tables — a ryph database URL:
#   pglite:./data/ryph     embedded PostgreSQL on disk (the default), survives restarts
#   pglite:memory://       embedded, throwaway — everything is gone on exit
#   postgres://…           a Postgres server
# All three are real PostgreSQL 17. Every module shares ONE connection to it: opening the same
# pglite data directory twice succeeds and then silently stops seeing its own writes.
# Provision the schema first: `bun run db:push` in this package, which covers every mounted
# module's tables, the historian's and memory's included.
#RYPH_DB=pglite:./data/ryph

# Gives the transcript firehose a database of its OWN. Unset (the default) shares RYPH_DB,
# which is the single-process posture: a second embedded instance costs a few hundred megabytes
# of memory the process never gets back, and under one Postgres the firehose and run-state are
# separate MVCC connections anyway. Set it, and provision it with
# `bun run db:push:history` in this package.
#RYPH_HISTORY_DB=pglite:./data/ryph-history

# ── Repository access ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two ways an agent can reach a repository, in order of least setup. Both go through the forge's
# git gateway; no run is ever handed a credential for a git host.
#
# 1. A repository ON THIS MACHINE, added in the UI under Repos → Connect repository → On this
#    machine. Runs clone it through the forge, and an approved patch lands as a branch in that
#    repository. No git host, no credential.
#
#    RYPH_LOCAL_REPO_ROOT is the directory such repositories may be added from: the line around
#    what this deployment may read off the disk. A setting of the forge's `local` provider, so it
#    only takes effect with RYPH_FORGE_URL=embedded (a standalone forge reads its own). Must be
#    an existing absolute directory; unset or `off`, no local repository can be added.
#RYPH_LOCAL_REPO_ROOT=/Users/me/code

# 2. A repository on a forge (RYPH_FORGE_URL below): GitHub, as an App or as you with a token
#    (RYPH_GITHUB_TOKEN / RYPH_GITHUB_TOKEN_COMMAND, read by the forge), GitLab, as a bot or as
#    you (RYPH_GITLAB_MODE=user with RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN / RYPH_GITLAB_TOKEN_COMMAND, plus
#    RYPH_GITLAB_URL for your own instance; packages/forge/.env.example), or Radicle. Approved
#    patches open as pull requests (GitHub), merge requests (GitLab) or patches (Radicle).

# 4. A Radicle repository, as YOU: `embedded` runs the Radicle bridge in this process over your
#    own identity and the radicle-node you already run (RAD_HOME, default ~/.radicle), beside the
#    in-process forge (RYPH_FORGE_URL=embedded). Connect a repository by its RID; only connected
#    ones are touched, and your node's seeding policies are left as they are. An encrypted key
#    signs through your ssh-agent (SSH_AUTH_SOCK). Its working files go to RYPH_RADICLE_DATA,
#    default ./data/radicle — never inside RAD_HOME. See packages/radicle's README, "User mode".
#RYPH_RADICLE_URL=embedded

# ── User-surface authentication ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single-user by default: the owner is made at boot and signs in by the login link printed then.
# `on` lets several people in; the first registration then needs the setup token from this log.
#RYPH_MULTIUSER=on
# The secret the app's server presents when it names a client address; the same value on the app.
# Unset, the address is taken from any caller (a run included), which can spend the owner's sign-in
# budget; the host warns at boot, and multi-user will not start at all. `./dev init` writes one.
RYPH_PROXY_SECRET=
# A script or curl uses an API token minted on the account page, exchanged at POST /v1/auth/token.
# Locked out? `ryph auth grant-owner <email>` on the host restores an owner without a listener.
# `off` opens the user surface entirely — local hacking only.
#RYPH_AUTH=off
# Outbound mail for verification and password-reset links: an SMTP URL and the From header.
# Both or neither. Unset, every such link is shown to an admin in the UI instead of mailed.
#RYPH_SMTP_URL=smtp://user:password@smtp.example.com:587
#RYPH_MAIL_FROM=ryph <ryph@example.com>

# ── Model access ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AES-GCM master key sealing PROVIDER KEYS: 64 hex chars, e.g. from `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Unset keeps model access and the data plane dark — agents with a model policy are refused.
#RYPH_SECRETS_KEY=
# The data plane's address AS SEEN FROM AN AGENT CONTAINER — the host cannot guess it.
# With docker on Docker Desktop this is usually host.docker.internal.
#RYPH_MODEL_PROXY_URL=http://host.docker.internal:7420
# Backstop lifetime of a run's virtual key; revocation on run conclusion is the primary cutoff.
#RYPH_VIRTUAL_KEY_TTL_MS=43200000
# The deployment's last line on model spend: a rolling ceiling in USD at list price, and its
# window in days. At it, every spending call is refused and no task can start. Unset, no ceiling.
#RYPH_MODEL_SPEND_CEILING_USD=
#RYPH_MODEL_SPEND_WINDOW_DAYS=30
# How long a run may sit past its spend cap before the proxy refuses its calls itself; the
# reaper cancels it at the cap first.
#RYPH_MODEL_SPEND_BACKSTOP_MS=30000

# ── Tool access (MCP) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The mcp-gateway's master key, sealing MCP SERVER CREDENTIALS — the third secret class. Unset
# means "the same key as RYPH_SECRETS_KEY", so tool access is on whenever model access is; set
# it separately only to keep a later split of the gateway from re-keying what it sealed.
#RYPH_MCP_KEY=
# The gateway data plane AS SEEN FROM AN AGENT CONTAINER — host.docker.internal under Desktop.
#RYPH_MCP_GATEWAY_URL=http://host.docker.internal:7430
# The interface that data plane BINDS. Loopback by default, and the only listener here that is:
# tool access rides RYPH_SECRETS_KEY unless RYPH_MCP_KEY is set, so this port would otherwise
# open on every interface the moment an existing deployment upgraded. Set it together with the
# URL above — a container view that the listener does not answer is the failure this pairing
# exists to prevent; `ryph config` shows both as resolved.
#RYPH_MCP_GATEWAY_HOST=0.0.0.0
# Where the gateway may dial. The default is public https hosts only: it forwards operator
# credentials to operator URLs, which makes it an SSRF target by construction. An MCP server
# running on this machine needs both of these; each is logged at boot when set.
#RYPH_MCP_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
#RYPH_MCP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_UPSTREAMS=1
# Backstop lifetime of a run's virtual MCP token; revocation on run conclusion is the primary cutoff.
#RYPH_MCP_VIRTUAL_KEY_TTL_MS=43200000
# Where a CUSTOM model endpoint may point. Set to 1 to let an admin register one at a loopback,
# link-local or private-range address — a LAN vLLM, and nothing else; plain http is permitted only
# for such an address. Off, a base URL must be https and must not literally name an address this
# machine answers on. Logged at boot when set, like its two neighbours above.
#RYPH_ALLOW_PRIVATE_MODEL_ENDPOINTS=1
# Hosted MCP servers (Tool servers → Add → From catalogue) run on the SAME backend as agents:
# RYPH_PROVISIONER=docker; under manual the catalogue says hosting is unavailable. Each is
# fronted by the tool guard, our own image — `bun run agent-image` builds it. The caps apply to every tool container unless its catalogue entry
# names its own memory; the supervisor probes healthy servers and retries unreachable ones.
#RYPH_TOOL_GUARD_IMAGE=ryph-tool-guard:dev
#RYPH_TOOL_MEMORY=512m
#RYPH_TOOL_CPUS=1
#RYPH_MCP_SUPERVISOR_INTERVAL_MS=30000

# ── Memory ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset (the default): @ryph/memory is mounted in-process over RYPH_DB — briefs are composed
# at task start, the management surface joins the control plane, and the memory tools reach agent
# containers through the gateway's platform server (so tool access above must be on for the
# tools; the brief rides without it). Set: a standalone memory service, dialed with the two
# tokens — the orchestrator's for composing briefs, the gateway's for forwarding tool calls.
#RYPH_MEMORY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7440
#RYPH_MEMORY_TOKEN=
#RYPH_MEMORY_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
# How often the in-process consolidator works the inbox.
#RYPH_MEMORY_CONSOLIDATE_INTERVAL_MS=60000

# ── Web (search and page reads) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @ryph/web is mounted in-process by default: `web__fetch` reads a public page as markdown, and
# `web__search` is offered ONLY when this deployment has a search key. Both reach agent
# containers through the gateway's platform server, so tool access above must be on. Every
# tool-capable agent's runs get them; an agent's tool policy may narrow it to one of the two.
# "off" takes the web tools away entirely: nothing mounted, no row seeded, and no run granted the
# row — including an agent whose own tool policy names it. A row a previous boot seeded stays in
# the database and still appears in the agent form (platform rows cannot be archived); it is the
# grant that goes, at every task start.
#RYPH_WEB_TOOLS=off
# A search key (Brave today). Unset: no `web__search` tool is offered at all.
#RYPH_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=brave
#RYPH_WEB_SEARCH_KEY=
# Permit plain http pages. Default: https only (and only the scheme's own port, 443 or 80).
#RYPH_WEB_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
# The whole of one page fetch, redirects included. The conversion's own budget is 5s, fixed.
#RYPH_WEB_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# Set: a STANDALONE web service the gateway dials, instead of the in-process mount.
#RYPH_WEB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7480
#RYPH_WEB_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# ── Forge (GitHub boundary) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The forge is its own process: `bun run --filter '@ryph/forge' dev` (port 7412), or
# `embedded` to mount it in this one. All three knobs unset: the forge surface is dark, no repo
# can be connected and no task can start.
# The forge as THIS process dials it (permission checks, PR submission, OAuth exchange).
# "noop" wires the recording fake — the whole patch lifecycle with no GitHub anywhere.
#RYPH_FORGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7412
# The git gateway AS AN AGENT CONTAINER dials it: every run clones through it with a run-scoped
# read-only key and its work leaves as a bundle — host.docker.internal under Desktop. Required
# with an http RYPH_FORGE_URL: the boot refuses a forge without it.
#RYPH_GIT_GATEWAY_URL=http://host.docker.internal:7412
# Shared service credential between the control plane and the forge — required with either URL
# above; also what mounts the /v1/forge/* surface.
#RYPH_FORGE_TOKEN=
# Forge tools: agents with a forge policy read and write issues and pull requests as the App.
# Set, the in-process gateway seeds the platform forge server and dials the forge's tool surface
# with this token — which the forge must be started with too. RYPH_FORGE_TOOLS_URL is where the
# gateway reaches it, when that is not RYPH_FORGE_URL.
#RYPH_FORGE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
#RYPH_FORGE_TOOLS_URL=
# Backstop lifetime of a run's git virtual key.
#RYPH_GIT_KEY_TTL_MS=86400000

# ── Provisioning runs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "manual" (the default) launches nothing and prints the env a hand-started runner needs;
# "docker" actually launches agent containers and needs the image below.
#RYPH_PROVISIONER=docker
# The image every run launches on, whatever its harness kind: it carries them all.
#RYPH_AGENT_IMAGE=ryph-agent:dev
# The browser sidecar a browser agent's run gets; unset, none does.
# docker and kubernetes (1.29+, native sidecars) launch it, each on top of the run's size class;
# a run that cannot get one starts without it. A digest-pinned image that will not pull holds a
# kubernetes run's pod, so push it first. Turning it on for an agent takes agents:policy.
#RYPH_BROWSER_IMAGE=ryph-browser:dev
# Docker leaves CPU and memory uncapped unless set; Kubernetes defaults to 1 CPU / 1536Mi.
#RYPH_BROWSER_CPUS=1
#RYPH_BROWSER_MEMORY=1536Mi
# The harness kinds an agent may be created with.
#RYPH_HARNESS_KINDS=pi,echo
# Size classes, name:key=value,…;name2:… with keys cpu, memory, ephemeral-storage, work-volume.
# An admin picks one per repo or workspace; RYPH_RUN_SIZE_DEFAULT (unset: the first) the rest.
# Docker defaults to bare standard (no CPU or memory caps); other backends use the size below.
# Host / Docker VM limits still apply. The run gate keeps its 1 CPU / 128Mi caps.
#RYPH_RUN_SIZES=standard:cpu=4,memory=8Gi,ephemeral-storage=10Gi
#RYPH_RUN_SIZE_DEFAULT=standard
# Environment builds. Off: every run uses RYPH_AGENT_IMAGE.
#RYPH_ENVIRONMENTS=off
# On a laptop the builder is the host's docker (it follows RYPH_PROVISIONER); no registry, the
# image stays in docker's store. The two images a build is made of are what `bun run
# agent-image` leaves behind, and unset they default to the agent image's siblings
# (ryph-agent:dev → ryph-harness:dev, ryph-universal:dev). RYPH_ENV_BUILD_PLATFORM pins the build's platform when those images
# are another architecture than this machine (e.g. linux/amd64 on Apple silicon).
#RYPH_ENV_BUILDER=docker
#RYPH_HARNESS_IMAGE=ryph-harness:dev
#RYPH_ENV_BASE_IMAGE=ryph-universal:dev
#RYPH_ENV_BUILD_PLATFORM=
# The git gateway as a build's clone dials it. The docker builder clones on this machine, where
# RYPH_GIT_GATEWAY_URL's container address does not resolve, so unset it uses RYPH_FORGE_URL, or
# the in-process forge on loopback.
#RYPH_ENV_GIT_GATEWAY_URL=
# Per-scope BuildKit caches, used where docker runs the containerd image store. Unset:
# ryph/environments under $XDG_CACHE_HOME, or under ~/.cache.
#RYPH_ENV_CACHE_DIR=
# Where a build's clone and image exports go while it runs (GBs). Unset: the system temp dir.
#RYPH_ENV_TEMP_DIR=
#RYPH_ENV_BUILD_TIMEOUT=60m
#RYPH_ENV_BUILD_CONCURRENCY=2
#RYPH_ENV_REBUILD_INTERVAL=6h
# Incremental builds in a row before the next is cold: each keeps what it rewrote on top of the
# last, so the cap bounds how far an image grows. 0 builds every image cold.
#RYPH_ENV_WARM_CHAIN=4
# Docker network to attach containers to.
#RYPH_DOCKER_NETWORK=
# The control plane's address as runners dial it — host.docker.internal again under Desktop.
#RYPH_PUBLIC_URL=http://host.docker.internal:7411
# The web app's origin as a browser reaches it: mailed links, run links in progress comments,
# and the passkey origin all derive from it. Unset, single-user defaults it to ./dev's vite
# server below (the owner's login link needs it); multi-user builds no link at all.
#RYPH_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ── Liveness timing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Silence longer than this marks a run lost.
#RYPH_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# How long a cancelled run may keep running before the reaper's kill.
#RYPH_CANCEL_GRACE_MS=120000
# Reaper sweep cadence.
#RYPH_REAPER_INTERVAL_MS=10000
# GitHub or GitLab user mode (no webhooks): how long after an answer an open pull or merge
# request is read again for a merge or close, and how many the submit sweep reads per tick (0
# switches the poll off). One whose patches closed is read every ten minutes for a week, whatever
# the interval. GitLab bot mode polls too, every ten minutes, for projects whose merge request
# events have not been heard; 0 per tick switches that fallback off as well.
#RYPH_MERGE_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
#RYPH_MERGE_POLL_PER_TICK=2

# ── Run limits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The ceiling every run is under; an agent's policy and a task's override lower it, never raise
# it. 0 is no cap. See the orchestrator's docs/development.md.
#RYPH_RUN_MAX_WALL_CLOCK_MS=43200000
#RYPH_RUN_MAX_SPEND_USD=
#RYPH_RUN_MAX_CALLS_IN_FLIGHT=8
# How many runs may be live at once across the deployment; unset is no cap.
#RYPH_RUN_CONCURRENCY=
# How many times one run may be issued a model credential.
#RYPH_RUN_MAX_CREDENTIALS=3

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# debug / info / warn / error / critical.
#RYPH_LOG_LEVEL=info
# json / text / colorful (default depends on whether stdout is a tty).
#RYPH_LOG_FORMAT=
